ues"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/joined(by:)-n00s":{"title":"joined(by:)","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/joined(by:)-n00s","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/joined(by:)-n00s","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"joined"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Separator"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"by"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Separator"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"JoinedBySequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:1